(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #135: the kernel's group meanings have their own
 forms. Signal 0 delivers nothing, so this is the only signal a test may
 send to a group or to everyone: it proves each form reaches kill(2)
 and clears the error flag. Process group 2147483647 does not exist
 (pids stop far below it), so that one fails with ESRCH, and a group
 only the running program knows to be 0 is refused before the kernel.)

Send signal 0 to my process group.
On error print "unexpected error on my process group".
Send signal 0 to every process.
On error print "unexpected error on every process".
Send signal 0 to process group 2147483647.
On error print "no process group 2147483647".
a number called leader is 1.
Set leader to 0.
Send signal 0 to process group leader.
On error print "process group 0 refused".
Print "done".
